// Fails about one run in three.
//
// THROW, not node.error(). A msg.error alone routes to catch without
// firing onComplete, so the span is never marked failed and this
// fixture would produce no error traces at all.
if (Math.random() < 0.33) {
    throw new Error('order failed validation: missing customer ref');
}
return msg;

// A second, differently-named failing step. Without this the
// operation breakdown would have one row and prove nothing.
if (Math.random() < 0.2) {
    throw new Error('ERP rejected the order');
}
return msg;

// Fails much more often than flow A, on purpose: the breakdown
// should rank this flow above the other, and a difference you can
// see beats two rows that look the same.
if (Math.random() < 0.6) {
    throw new Error('invoice template missing for this customer');
}
return msg;
